WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.740
Good to have you on Tesla's short time, episode 541 for July 14th, 2026.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:12.200
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver. Plenty going on in EV land. Let's get to it.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:17.560
Tesla's European FSD fleet passed 50 million kilometers in under three months,

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.140
handing regulators in Germany and France the real world data they have been waiting for.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:28.360
Dutch owners logged over 10 million kilometers within a month of provisional approval in April.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.480
Lithuania, Estonia, Denmark and Belgium added approvals through June.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.200
The combined fleet passed 50 million kilometers by July 14th.

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:44.940
Owners are averaging nearly 580,000 FSD kilometers daily across five countries.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:52.340
The data set now covers narrow roads and heavy cyclist traffic that regulators in larger markets want to see.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:58.760
Italy, Germany and France are evaluating next-stage approvals on the basis of these edge case

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:06.160
miles. Tesla has formally applied for FSD supervised approval in Italy as the sixth European country.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:11.860
Approval there would extend contiguous coverage and add another high mileage market to the

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:18.040
growing data set. From regulatory data collection, we turn to the hardware that will eventually run on

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:24.820
that data. Samsung Foundry confirmed the AI5 chip tape out has completed. Production will begin

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:32.020
at its Texas facility. The next generation inference silicon targets both unsupervised FSD and

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:41.240
Optimus. The move advances the HW5-slash AI5 timeline tracked since early 2026. Focus now shifts

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:46.560
from design validation to the first wafers that will determine whether the new silicon meets the

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:52.340
required performance multiplier. That brings us to the dedicated energy cells supporting the broader

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:59.660
ecosystem. Samsung SDI will construct a dedicated production line for Tesla Energy Storage System batteries

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:06.840
in the United States. The line focuses on megapack scale products. No capacity figures or timeline

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:13.460
were provided. The dedicated line separates stationary storage manufacturing from vehicle cell lines.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:19.660
Each track can optimize for different cycle life and cost targets without competing for the same factory

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:26.660
capacity. Tesla first principles explores why a dedicated U.S. battery line for megapacks changes

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:32.020
capital allocation and raw material contracting compared with shared vehicle cell production.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:38.680
Battery supply chains have long been viewed as a single bottleneck that any manufacturer must either

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:46.020
own or endure. Tesla's decision to have Samsung SDI build a dedicated U.S. line for energy storage

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:51.580
cells shows the company treating stationary batteries as a separate production track rather than a

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:58.380
side stream of vehicle cells. This separation lets each product chase its own cost curve and chemistry

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:03.540
without forcing trade-offs in energy density or cycle life that vehicle packs demand.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:10.420
The practical result is faster scaling of megapack output while vehicle programs continue to absorb

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:17.760
4680 and LFP cells at their own pace. It also reduces the risk that a sudden surge in car

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:22.480
demand crowds out grid projects that now contribute meaningful revenue and margin.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:29.480
Over time, the split could matter more than vertical integration itself. A dedicated storage line

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:35.660
lets Tesla negotiate raw material contracts sized to predictable utility demand instead of the

00:03:35.660 --> 00:03:41.760
lumpier vehicle schedule. That predictability feeds back into lower financing costs for the factories

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:47.560
that build the factories. From stationary energy scaling, we move to the vehicles that will move

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:54.760
goods using that same energy infrastructure. ATC logistics will run 20 Tesla semis at the LA and

00:03:54.920 --> 00:04:01.700
Long Beach ports starting early 2027. The trucks will charge at Forum Mobility's new FM Santa

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:08.380
Fay Depot in Rancho Dominguez. The semis 500 mile range and megawatt charging system are the

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:14.620
key reasons cited for the choice over diesel. Three other fleets have already signed similar deals with

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:21.360
Forum Mobility for the same routes. Paper transport will test the long-range semi-configuration in

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:27.740
dedicated operations around Chicago. The colder weather routes will provide data on real world

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:34.340
range and charging performance in winter conditions. Chicago's combination of cold temperatures and frequent

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:40.260
short haul cycles will test whether the 500 mile rating holds when auxiliary loads for cabin heat

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:45.940
and battery conditioning are highest. From freight movement, we shift to the charging network that will

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:52.920
support both freight and passenger vehicles. 7-11 Japan will install superchargers at select locations

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:59.180
across the country. The move expands Tesla's charging network into high traffic retail sites that

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:05.340
already serve millions of daily customers. No timeline or number of sites was disclosed. The

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:11.060
partnership places chargers where convenience store foot traffic is highest. Utilization could

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:16.740
increase during evening and overnight hours when other sites see lower demand. From physical

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:22.620
charging access, we turn to the regulatory path for the vehicles that will eventually use it unsupervised.

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:29.340
Tesla confirmed that employees have begun riding in cyber cab vehicles. The internal program marks

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:35.900
the first documented use of the vehicle without a safety driver in controlled conditions. No details

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:41.820
on frequency or route types were shared. The step moves the program from static demonstrations to

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:48.440
supervised passenger miles inside company gates. This is the necessary precursor before any public

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:54.960
unsupervised deployment can be requested. From the standard cyber cab, we turn to the accessible

00:05:54.960 --> 00:06:01.340
variant being developed in parallel. Tesla confirmed development of a wheelchair accessible version

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:06.840
of the RoboTaxi. The variant is intended to broaden the addressable market for the upcoming

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:13.440
autonomous vehicle. No production timeline or additional specifications were released. Adding

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:19.620
accessibility features early in the design cycle avoids costly retrofits later. The approach

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:25.560
positions the vehicle for regulatory and municipal fleet contracts that require ADA compliance.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:31.820
From vehicle development, we turn to the competitive pressure building in the same regulatory markets.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:38.580
Ex-panging is expanding its camera-only autonomous driving system into Europe. The company follows

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:43.800
the same vision-only approach Tesla uses and has already begun regulatory discussions.

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:50.660
No specific launch markets or timelines were named. The parallel technical strategy sets up direct

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:56.840
competition for the same regulatory approvals and driver datasets that Tesla is currently accumulating

00:06:56.840 --> 00:07:05.100
across five EU countries. California signed a $270 million EV rebate program into law that begins

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:12.180
this summer. Tesla vehicles qualify under the new rules for first-time buyers. The program targets price

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:18.220
reductions for qualifying electric vehicles sold in the state. Eligibility gives Tesla an immediate

00:07:18.220 --> 00:07:24.780
price advantage in the largest USEV market, just as competing models face tighter inventory and

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:31.300
slower sales. A large South African farm installed five megawatts of solar paired with battery storage

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:38.600
equivalent to 1,481 power walls. The system allows the operation to disconnect from the national

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:46.360
utility ESCOM entirely. No further details on payback period or installer were released. The installation

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:51.740
demonstrates how scaled residential-style battery blocks can support commercial loads that previously

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:58.700
required grid connection. Tesla Roddy is preparing to drive coast to coast using the latest FSD

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:04.340
version. The trip will test how the system handles long distance routing and varied highway

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:10.100
conditions without intervention. No start date has been announced yet. The planned route will expose

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:15.820
the software to construction zones, weather changes, and rest area navigation that shorter tests

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:24.140
rarely capture in a single continuous drive. Version 14.3.5 introduces a live camera preview window

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:30.580
for drivers. The feature shows what the vehicle's vision system is seeing in real-time. It is intended

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:37.500
to increase transparency during supervised operation. Drivers can now watch the same visual input the

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:43.740
neural net uses, offering a direct view into why the car chooses certain maneuvers. Early users

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:51.400
report that version 14.3.5 struggles with parking maneuvers in some lots. The issues appear most

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:58.020
noticeable when pulling into tight or angled spaces. Tesla has not yet commented on a fixed timeline.

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:03.380
The feedback loop from these early reports will determine whether the next point release addresses

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:10.120
parking before wider distribution or waits for additional fleet data. Tesla stated that its vehicles

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:16.960
can last beyond 15 years at 20,000 kilometers of annual driving. The claim is based on internal

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:23.540
durability testing and fleet data. It positions Tesla vehicles as long-term ownership options rather

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:30.160
than short cycle fleet cars. The durability statement supplies a concrete benchmark for residual value

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:36.580
calculations that used car buyers and leasing companies have been requesting. Now, one thing worth

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:43.600
watching is the sharpest used EV price falls among major brands. Used Tesla values have fallen

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:51.040
10%, the steepest drop among major EV brands. The decline reflects higher inventory levels and buyer

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:58.360
hesitation ahead of newer model launches. Tesla's position as the largest used EV seller makes it the

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:04.160
most visible barometer of softening demand in the segment. Dealers report that the price pressure

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:12.620
is most pronounced on 2023-2024 model Y units, where supply from lease returns and trade-ins has

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:18.960
outpaced retail absorption in several European markets. Tomorrow, we'll be watching for the first

